WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.801
We've got some breaking news right now.

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:04.170
The Colorado Supreme Court, get this,

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.172
has just ruled on a challenge

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:06.940
to Donald Trump's

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:09.943
appearance on the state's 2024 ballot.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.077
I want to go straight to CNN's

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.012
Paula Reid Paula.

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.713
What does this ruling say?

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:13.880
Well,

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.681
if this is a stunning

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.116
ruling from the Colorado

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:17.617
Supreme Court saying

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:18.151
that Trump

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:21.988
should not appear on the ballot in 2024.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:23.790
Now, this is surprising in part

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.793
because they are reversing a lower court

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.294
that found while Trump

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.330
did engage in an insurrection

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.931
on January six,

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:32.766
that Section

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.734
three of the 14th Amendment

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.470
did not apply to presidents,

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:37.971
and therefore

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:40.573
he should not be kept off the ballot.

00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:41.841
Now, when we're talking about

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:42.976
this particular section,

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.411
this is a civil war

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.579
era clause of the Constitution.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:47.313
And in here

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.948
the courts are trying to assess

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.617
exactly what that means.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:53.653
Well, it does specifically mention House

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.588
representatives, the Senate,

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:56.790
even electors.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.692
It doesn't say anything about president.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:00.093
So here

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:01.194
the court was weighing

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:02.462
whether they could

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:03.596
keep former President

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.331
Trump off the ballot

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:07.333
because of what happened on January six.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:07.600
And here,

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.401
the Supreme Court,

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.035
the highest court

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:10.703
in the state of Colorado,

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:13.239
ruling that he should be disqualified,

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.908
he should be kept off the ballot.

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:15.775
But, Wolf,

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:17.977
they're going to stay or pause

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.112
this decision

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:21.181
until January 4th

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:22.482
to allow the former president

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:23.950
or anyone else to appeal

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.252
to the Supreme Court on this question.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.420
Very significant indeed.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.922
I want to bring in the rest of our team

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.256
right now, Ellie Hoenig.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:33.493
How stunning is this decision?

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.528
Well, Wolf, this is a historic decision.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.097
It's a momentous decision

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:39.032
as the Supreme Court itself says.

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.900
They are in uncharted territory here.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.969
But it's really important to keep in mind

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.771
this is not the last word here.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.206
This is almost certainly

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:47.273
going up to the U.S.

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:47.907
Supreme Court,

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.442
which can review the decisions

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:50.910
of a state Supreme court.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.412
In fact, the Colorado Supreme Court

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.214
anticipates that possibility.

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:55.281
And for that reason,

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.317
they put their own ruling on hold

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.052
until January 4th,

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.520
anticipating that it will go

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.921
up to the Supreme Court.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.256
The practical consequence

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.090
as it stands

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:04.891
at this moment,

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.059
though, is that Donald Trump

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:08.194
will not be on the Colorado

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:11.164
ballot in the race for president in 2024.

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:11.831
The Supreme Court

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:13.533
almost certainly will take this up.

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.267
It's also important

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.034
to keep in mind

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.202
for the broader context,

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.370
there have been dozens

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.571
of these challenges

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:21.441
filed across the country, and 18

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:22.542
or so of them have either

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:23.776
failed, been rejected

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.578
or been withdrawn by the plaintiffs.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.881
So this is really an outlier.

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:28.715
The Supreme Court

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.350
is going to have the final say.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.551
The consequences here are,

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.286
of course, enormous normalizing.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:37.924
Are you surprised by this decision?

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:40.093
Well, Wolf, the

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:43.863
law and really

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.732
politics have collided.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:49.736
And in this instance, law has won.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.038
There is a logic to the decision.

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.940
The 14th Amendment provides

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.009
is that this direction is

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.011
may not hold office.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:58.912
The lower court

00:02:58.912 --> 00:02:59.746
found

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:01.514
that Donald Trump had engaged

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.650
in insurrectionist activity

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:05.084
excuse consonant with what

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:08.321
the January six committee found.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:11.891
And so the only question was legally,

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.693
did this apply to a president?

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.662
The Supreme Court said it did.

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.263
I think because of the earth

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:20.266
shaking nature of the holding,

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.901
we thought that

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:24.237
politics might militate against it.

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:26.573
But the courts, as they should

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:28.141
do, have put on blinkers

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.776
and applied the Constitution.

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:31.878
Now it'll be up to the Supreme Court

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.313
to have the final word.

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.248
Yeah, the 14th Amendment to the U.S.

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:36.082
Constitution

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.383
says, and I'm quoting now,

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.886
No person shall hold any office

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.821
who, having previously taken an oath

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:42.655
to support

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.490
the Constitution of the United States,

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.658
shall have engaged

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:46.960
shall have engaged

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.962
in insurrection or rebellion

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:49.862
against the same

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:50.730
or given aid

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:53.733
or comfort to the enemies thereof.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.001
Pretty significant.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:57.837
14th Amendment to the U.S. Constitution.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:00.006
David, this has never happened before.

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.140
Earlier challenges

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.475
to get Trump removed

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:04.510
from state ballots for the presidency,

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.279
for the presidency have failed.

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.214
What does it mean politically for Trump

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:09.015
to be removed

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.883
potentially from the Republican

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:13.052
primary ballot in Colorado?

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:13.553
Yeah, Wolf,

00:04:13.553 --> 00:04:14.287
I think we're going to go through

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:15.755
a year of this has never happened

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:17.390
before in this presidential election.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:20.393
So be prepared to keep stating that.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:21.127
You know, as L.Z.

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:21.628
was noting,

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:23.229
and I do think it is important context

00:04:23.229 --> 00:04:24.530
you're bringing up here,

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.634
the vast majority of these cases to date

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.636
have actually gone the other way.

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:31.137
And I would imagine

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:32.438
that that is not going to be lost

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:33.239
on the Supreme Court

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:34.073
when it looks

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:36.075
at the specifics of this case, but

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:38.311
looks at this issue broadly.

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:39.245
Politically, of course,

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:41.547
Colorado has ten electoral votes.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.216
They were in Joe Biden's column,

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:46.986
not Donald Trump's column back in 2020.

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:49.889
But if you start taking potentially

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:52.892
available electoral votes off the board,

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:55.028
the map to to 70,

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:55.795
even though this was not

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:56.763
part of this 2020

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:58.064
path becomes

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:00.033
more complicated in that way.

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:01.367
We have no indication yet

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.101
that the Trump team

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.603
was planning to engage

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:05.405
fully in Colorado and

00:05:05.405 --> 00:05:07.874
and run a concerted effort

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:08.908
in that state

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:10.777
to play for those electoral votes.

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:13.246
But again, it's the broader concept here

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.947
that would be earthshaking

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:17.116
to the election itself.

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:20.119
And as we learned back in 2000,

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.120
in Bush v Gore,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:21.321
you know,

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:22.689
when the Supreme Court gets involved,

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:25.692
looking at a state Supreme Court,

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:26.826
things unexpected

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:28.628
could could potentially happen.

00:05:28.628 --> 00:05:29.362
And we'll see

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:30.496
what the Supreme Court does here.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.065
This is always been an issue

00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:32.999
that's going to be headed

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:33.666
for the highest court,

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:34.967
because earlier efforts

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:35.601
to get Trump

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:36.703
removed from the state

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:39.372
presidential ballot failed in Minnesota,

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:41.107
in New Hampshire, in Michigan,

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:42.475
and right now in Colorado.

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:44.210
It's going forward to remove him.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:44.577
Elissa,

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:46.579
how do you expect Trump and his team

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:49.048
to react to this stunning news?

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:50.683
It truly is stunning news,

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:52.685
and I expect this is a five alarm fire

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:54.287
even to the fact of Dave Collins

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:54.887
point that

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:55.788
this doesn't actually

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:57.423
really change the map for Donald Trump.

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:58.424
He's not necessarily

00:05:58.424 --> 00:05:59.258
playing for the ten

00:05:59.258 --> 00:06:00.760
electoral votes in Colorado,

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.161
but it's the precedent it sets.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:02.595
And it's also

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:03.496
just the mindset

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:04.831
that it signals to voters,

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.632
which is for the first time in history,

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:08.668
he is unfit to appear on a ballot

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:10.203
for the presidency.

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:10.770
And of course,

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:11.804
there would be implications

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:14.040
if the Supreme Court upheld this.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:14.874
I think that you're going

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:16.642
to hear a massive outcry

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:17.877
from him and his team

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:19.512
there needlessly to say, needless

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:21.247
to say, are going to be challenging this.

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:22.982
And I do offer a word of caution

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:23.750
because these

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:24.851
these have obviously appeared

00:06:24.851 --> 00:06:25.551
in other states

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:27.420
and mostly been struck down.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.155
There is an argument to be made

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:30.923
for the fact that this should ultimately,

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.725
ultimately be left up to the voters.

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:33.326
I've heard this from

00:06:33.326 --> 00:06:34.727
quite a few Republicans

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:35.628
who want to see us

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:37.029
move on from Donald Trump,

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:38.398
but they worry about playing

00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:39.232
into the hands of him

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:40.733
being able to say the system is rigged.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:41.367
Now, it's not.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:42.301
This is the courts working.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.003
They're the way they're supposed to.

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:45.371
But he will quickly frame this

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:46.572
as they're rigging the system

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:48.040
against me in favor of Joe Biden.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.575
Watch for him to say that.

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:50.643
Let's get back to Paula.

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:51.644
So what comes next?

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:53.212
Walk us through the process.

00:06:53.212 --> 00:06:54.847
I assume Trump and his lawyers

00:06:54.847 --> 00:06:57.083
will start to appeal this, right? Yeah.

00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:58.985
Unfortunately for Trump's legal team,

00:06:58.985 --> 00:07:00.319
they are likely going to have to work

00:07:00.319 --> 00:07:01.254
through the holiday.

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:03.423
Something that they had complained about

00:07:03.423 --> 00:07:03.990
are related

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.858
to the special counsel investigation

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:07.326
and the filing deadlines there.

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:07.860
And some of the work

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.295
that the special counsel they said

00:07:09.295 --> 00:07:11.063
was making them do through the holiday.

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:12.165
But here this is going to

00:07:12.165 --> 00:07:12.932
this is going to be something

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:13.232
that they're going

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:14.667
to have to pay attention to.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:16.536
They're literally being given a window

00:07:16.536 --> 00:07:17.970
in which to appeal this

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:19.238
to the Supreme Court.

00:07:19.238 --> 00:07:20.273
We would fully expect that

00:07:20.273 --> 00:07:22.208
they will avail themselves of that.

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:23.676
And then this case,

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:25.445
it is likely that the Supreme Court

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:28.080
would want to take up this question

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:28.581
of exactly

00:07:28.581 --> 00:07:30.716
who the 14th Amendment applies to

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:31.751
and if

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:33.152
Trump or any other current

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:35.521
or former president can be removed

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:36.589
from the ballot here.

00:07:36.589 --> 00:07:38.991
And while this only applies to Colorado,

00:07:38.991 --> 00:07:40.293
this is something that will likely

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:41.661
have reverberations

00:07:41.661 --> 00:07:42.695
in other states

00:07:42.695 --> 00:07:44.597
that are considering the same issue.

00:07:44.597 --> 00:07:45.832
I also want to note that

00:07:45.832 --> 00:07:46.966
some people may wonder, well,

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:48.034
if he's not on the ballot,

00:07:48.034 --> 00:07:49.802
can people just write him in?

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:51.270
Well, in this opinion,

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:52.605
they specifically say

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:53.773
that the secretary of state

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:56.509
is also barred from counting

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:59.745
any write in votes cast for Trump.

00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:00.580
Interesting.

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:01.013
Ellie,

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:03.149
why is the Colorado Supreme Court

00:08:03.149 --> 00:08:05.051
right now an outlier here?

00:08:05.051 --> 00:08:06.419
Minnesota, as I pointed out,

00:08:06.419 --> 00:08:09.121
dismissed a similar lawsuit to this one

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:12.158
back in November.

00:08:12.225 --> 00:08:12.992
Well, Wolf, this is

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:14.093
precisely why

00:08:14.093 --> 00:08:15.695
we have such dissonance

00:08:15.695 --> 00:08:16.796
in the various decisions

00:08:16.796 --> 00:08:18.498
that we're getting from different states,

00:08:18.498 --> 00:08:20.233
because nobody quite knows

00:08:20.233 --> 00:08:22.568
exactly how the 14th Amendment works.

00:08:22.568 --> 00:08:23.970
Yes, we have this amendment.

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:24.704
It's very important.

00:08:24.704 --> 00:08:26.205
It says that anyone who gave aid

00:08:26.205 --> 00:08:28.508
to insurrection, rebellion is ineligible.

00:08:28.508 --> 00:08:29.509
But the problem is

00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:30.710
neither the Constitution

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:31.777
nor Congress

00:08:31.777 --> 00:08:33.446
have given us any further guidance

00:08:33.446 --> 00:08:34.280
as to how it works.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.548
And so the theories

00:08:35.548 --> 00:08:37.483
that have been advanced by 14th Amendment

00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:39.585
proponents have been all over the map.

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:40.119
Literally.

00:08:40.119 --> 00:08:41.921
They argued at one point that, well,

00:08:41.921 --> 00:08:42.989
it's up to individual

00:08:42.989 --> 00:08:44.023
secretaries of state.

00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:45.391
They can decide on their own

00:08:45.391 --> 00:08:46.592
while every secretary

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:47.927
of state, Democrat and Republican,

00:08:47.927 --> 00:08:49.562
to consider that rejected it.

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:50.196
Then they went into

00:08:50.196 --> 00:08:51.631
various courts, sometimes

00:08:51.631 --> 00:08:53.766
state level, sometimes federal level.

00:08:53.766 --> 00:08:55.735
And the failures have across the board

00:08:55.735 --> 00:08:57.870
been not so much failures of proving

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.972
that Donald Trump was in fact aiding

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:01.707
or engaging in insurrection.

00:09:01.707 --> 00:09:03.376
But procedural questions of

00:09:03.376 --> 00:09:04.810
how do we make this decision?

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.812
Who decides? Is it a judge?

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:07.880
Is it a jury?

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:09.448
What burden of proof?

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:10.249
And the Colorado

00:09:10.249 --> 00:09:12.084
Supreme Court satisfies itself

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:12.752
that what was done

00:09:12.752 --> 00:09:14.520
here in the trial court, the trial court

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.122
judge held a several week

00:09:16.122 --> 00:09:18.224
long hearing was enough

00:09:18.224 --> 00:09:19.892
and that the law is clear enough

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:20.993
that they made this decision.

00:09:20.993 --> 00:09:22.728
But that's going to be the question

00:09:22.728 --> 00:09:23.763
for the Supreme Court.

00:09:23.763 --> 00:09:25.264
I don't think it will so much be

00:09:25.264 --> 00:09:27.366
did Donald Trump engage in insurrection?

00:09:27.366 --> 00:09:28.267
I think it will be.

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:29.969
Is there an established procedure

00:09:29.969 --> 00:09:30.903
and doesn't violate

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:32.738
Donald Trump's due process rights

00:09:32.738 --> 00:09:34.574
to essentially make one up on the fly

00:09:34.574 --> 00:09:36.709
and then apply it backwards in time?

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:37.310
Norm,

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:38.311
do you think this ruling

00:09:38.311 --> 00:09:39.879
by the Colorado Supreme Court

00:09:39.879 --> 00:09:44.116
will ultimately stand?

00:09:44.216 --> 00:09:44.817
Well, Wolf,

00:09:44.817 --> 00:09:45.918
that'll be up to

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:47.019
the United States

00:09:47.019 --> 00:09:48.821
Supreme Court, of course.

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:51.424
But I think that this is one

00:09:51.424 --> 00:09:53.926
of the more substantial of the cases.

00:09:53.926 --> 00:09:56.462
Ellie is talking about a very deal,

00:09:56.462 --> 00:09:57.063
but very

00:09:57.063 --> 00:09:58.030
small number

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:00.600
that have been queued up at trial,

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.901
gone up on appeal,

00:10:01.901 --> 00:10:03.169
been fully briefed

00:10:03.169 --> 00:10:05.237
with an evidentiary basis.

00:10:05.237 --> 00:10:06.305
And when you just

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:08.007
look at the plain language

00:10:08.007 --> 00:10:09.976
of the 14th Amendment,

00:10:09.976 --> 00:10:12.445
you put that together with what

00:10:12.445 --> 00:10:14.013
the January six committee

00:10:14.013 --> 00:10:15.348
found, the testimony

00:10:15.348 --> 00:10:16.082
and the evidence

00:10:16.082 --> 00:10:19.952
that were taken by the trial court here,

00:10:20.019 --> 00:10:22.321
the trial court found with merit

00:10:22.321 --> 00:10:25.725
that Donald Trump insurrection

00:10:25.725 --> 00:10:29.762
and the government is not going to be so

00:10:29.862 --> 00:10:30.930
easily dismissed.

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:32.798
I think the Supreme Court

00:10:32.798 --> 00:10:33.799
will wrestle with it.

00:10:33.799 --> 00:10:35.701
They'll take it seriously.

00:10:35.701 --> 00:10:36.669
And it's very tough

00:10:36.669 --> 00:10:37.970
to predict what they'll do.

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:39.472
But it is necessary

00:10:39.472 --> 00:10:42.975
as a well-founded legal evidence

00:10:42.975 --> 00:10:43.876
for pre-testing.

